WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.352 --> 00:00:01.791
This is Limit Orders.

2
00:00:01.791 --> 00:00:07.045
It lists every limit order resting on your exchanges, and it's where you place new

3
00:00:07.045 --> 00:00:11.978
ones, from a single order to a staggered ladder spread across a price range.

4
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:16.088
A limit order waits until the market reaches your price.

5
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:20.077
Buys rest below the current price, and sells rest above it.

6
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:25.324
The table is split into buys and sells, with a count on each tab.

7
00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.890
The New order button follows the tab you're on.

8
00:00:28.579 --> 00:00:32.600
Each row shows the account, pair, limit price, volume, and

9
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.760
how much has filled, with a partial tag if some has traded.

10
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.271
Estimated total is the limit price times the volume.

11
00:00:40.961 --> 00:00:45.286
Click a column heading to sort by it, and click again to flip the order.

12
00:00:45.286 --> 00:00:48.544
By default, the newest orders sit at the top.

13
00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:55.532
The filter box narrows the table by pair or order ID, and the counts on the tabs follow it.

14
00:00:56.219 --> 00:01:00.690
With All Exchanges selected, a second menu shows a single account.

15
00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.390
Clear them both, and everything comes back.

16
00:01:04.053 --> 00:01:07.845
Click a row for the full details: what has filled, what's

17
00:01:07.845 --> 00:01:10.971
left, when it was opened, and its complete ID.

18
00:01:10.971 --> 00:01:15.333
This view is read only, so just looking can never cancel anything.

19
00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:19.470
To cancel an order, use the Cancel button on its row.

20
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.339
Cyrus asks you to confirm, because it can't be undone.

21
00:01:23.339 --> 00:01:27.196
On a partly filled order, only the remainder is cancelled.

22
00:01:27.196 --> 00:01:28.339
We'll keep this one.

23
00:01:29.028 --> 00:01:30.521
Now let's build a ladder.

24
00:01:30.521 --> 00:01:34.457
On the Sell tab, the button becomes New sell limit order.

25
00:01:34.457 --> 00:01:37.409
Click it, and a three-step wizard opens.

26
00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:40.159
Step one is what and where.

27
00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:45.584
The side comes from the tab you were on, and Exchange picks which account places the orders.

28
00:01:45.584 --> 00:01:48.111
Here, that's Main, on Kraken.

29
00:01:48.803 --> 00:01:52.543
When you're selling, the coin list only offers coins you hold.

30
00:01:52.543 --> 00:01:57.556
When you're buying, it also lists coins the exchange trades that you don't hold yet.

31
00:01:57.556 --> 00:01:58.992
We'll sell some SOL.

32
00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.934
Order style is Single or Staggered.

33
00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:05.617
Single places one order at a price and amount you choose.

34
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:10.232
Staggered spreads one total across several orders at different prices.

35
00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:15.222
Then pick one or more trading pairs, each showing your balance.

36
00:02:15.222 --> 00:02:23.333
With more than one, the steps take turns: the first on USD, the next on USDC, then back to USD.

37
00:02:23.992 --> 00:02:25.032
Click Next.

38
00:02:25.032 --> 00:02:28.051
Step two shows the market price for each pair.

39
00:02:28.051 --> 00:02:32.463
Number of steps is how many orders to make, up to fifty per selected

40
00:02:32.463 --> 00:02:36.096
pair, and the hint says how long they'll take to place.

41
00:02:36.778 --> 00:02:39.970
The price band sets how far from the market the ladder

42
00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.513
sits, here two to twelve percent above it.

43
00:02:42.513 --> 00:02:47.969
Cyrus splits the band into equal slices, one per step, and picks a random price

44
00:02:47.969 --> 00:02:53.217
inside each, so the ladder stays in order and no step can cross the market.

45
00:02:53.892 --> 00:02:58.603
Exact prices lets you type the range yourself, starting from the band you set.

46
00:02:58.603 --> 00:03:02.552
For a sell, the second price must be higher than the first.

47
00:03:02.552 --> 00:03:04.241
We'll stay with percentages.

48
00:03:04.922 --> 00:03:09.114
Total to use is the share of your free balance the ladder can commit.

49
00:03:09.114 --> 00:03:12.266
Coins already tied up in other orders don't count.

50
00:03:12.266 --> 00:03:14.965
The line underneath shows what that works out to.

51
00:03:15.639 --> 00:03:21.799
Cyrus also checks that every step clears the exchange's minimum order size and value.

52
00:03:21.799 --> 00:03:26.533
If your balance can't stretch that far, it tells you how many steps it can cover.

53
00:03:27.215 --> 00:03:29.333
Post-only is on by default.

54
00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:33.632
If the market has already reached your price, the order is rejected

55
00:03:33.632 --> 00:03:37.418
rather than filled, so you pay maker fees, not taker fees.

56
00:03:38.105 --> 00:03:43.380
Click Next, and step three lists every order before anything is sent: the

57
00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:48.294
pair, price, amount, estimated total, and distance from the market.

58
00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:53.374
Amounts are rounded down, so the ladder never adds up to more than you set aside.

59
00:03:54.062 --> 00:03:58.507
Every price and amount can be edited, and the cross removes a step.

60
00:03:58.507 --> 00:04:02.244
A step that can't be placed, say it's under the exchange's

61
00:04:02.244 --> 00:04:06.047
minimum, is outlined in red, with the reason listed below.

62
00:04:06.047 --> 00:04:09.238
Nothing is sent until every step is valid.

63
00:04:09.904 --> 00:04:13.204
Regenerate prices draws a new random price inside

64
00:04:13.204 --> 00:04:16.370
each slice, and keeps any amounts you changed.

65
00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:19.149
Reset rebuilds the ladder from step two.

66
00:04:19.822 --> 00:04:24.120
Open Advanced to shape how the total is spread, one bar per step.

67
00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.315
Presets cover the common shapes.

68
00:04:26.315 --> 00:04:29.380
Far out puts more on the steps furthest from the

69
00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.445
market: better prices, but less likely to fill.

70
00:04:33.135 --> 00:04:37.437
Drag the bright line to move the price level that half the volume sits

71
00:04:37.437 --> 00:04:41.862
within, or use the slider to bunch it together or push it to both ends.

72
00:04:41.862 --> 00:04:45.080
Reshaping only moves volume between steps.

73
00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.463
It never adds any.

74
00:04:47.151 --> 00:04:51.157
Orders go out one at a time, paced to suit the exchange.

75
00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:56.436
You can leave this page meanwhile, but closing Cyrus stops the rest from being sent.

76
00:04:56.436 --> 00:04:58.471
When you're happy, click Place.

77
00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.863
A progress panel appears above the table.

78
00:05:01.863 --> 00:05:08.046
Each order moves from queued, to placing, to placed, with its order ID alongside.

79
00:05:08.711 --> 00:05:13.249
While it runs, new batches have to wait, and Stop halts the rest.

80
00:05:13.249 --> 00:05:18.142
Anything already placed stays on the exchange, and you'd cancel it from the table.

81
00:05:18.826 --> 00:05:20.319
You don't have to wait here.

82
00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:24.827
On any other page, the pill in the top bar keeps track of the batch.

83
00:05:24.827 --> 00:05:26.515
Click it to come straight back.

84
00:05:27.195 --> 00:05:30.709
Here, the demo rejects two orders on purpose.

85
00:05:30.709 --> 00:05:36.570
A rejected order shows the exchange's reason, and the rest carry on, unless the problem

86
00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:41.892
would sink them all, like invalid keys, a rate limit, or running out of funds.

87
00:05:42.561 --> 00:05:45.224
Dismiss clears the panel and the pill.

88
00:05:45.224 --> 00:05:49.040
Back on the Sell tab, the new orders are at the top of the table.

89
00:05:49.732 --> 00:05:54.084
Further down, a chart shows what each coin is being sold into.

90
00:05:54.084 --> 00:05:58.162
Each bar is one pair on one account, sized by what it would pay

91
00:05:58.162 --> 00:06:01.916
out, in that pair's currency, if every order on it fills.

92
00:06:02.592 --> 00:06:06.132
Below that, a histogram shows where one pair's orders

93
00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:09.071
sit by price, with the market price marked.

94
00:06:09.071 --> 00:06:14.204
Here's SOL to USD, with the new ladder stepping up above the market.

95
00:06:14.879 --> 00:06:19.763
The line underneath says how far the price has to move before half of it fills.

96
00:06:19.763 --> 00:06:22.395
Hover a bar to see the orders inside it.

97
00:06:23.083 --> 00:06:24.722
Now let's cancel the ladder.

98
00:06:24.722 --> 00:06:29.283
Back at the top, tick each new order, and a bar appears with a count.

99
00:06:29.283 --> 00:06:32.528
The header box ticks every row the filter is showing.

100
00:06:33.207 --> 00:06:39.620
A selection only covers rows you can see, so a bulk cancel never reaches anything off screen.

101
00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:44.088
Click Cancel, and every order is listed in full before you confirm.

102
00:06:44.764 --> 00:06:48.177
Confirm, and they're cancelled one at a time, about

103
00:06:48.177 --> 00:06:51.323
a second apart, each row reporting its result.

104
00:06:51.323 --> 00:06:54.062
Any that fail stay ticked so you can try again.

105
00:06:54.062 --> 00:06:57.786
These all went through, so the dialog closes on its own.

106
00:06:58.464 --> 00:07:04.717
Export CSV saves every buy and sell order matching your filters as a spreadsheet.

107
00:07:04.717 --> 00:07:08.909
Sells priced in dollars also get a cost basis and an estimated

108
00:07:08.909 --> 00:07:12.762
gain, using the lot matching method from the Taxes page.

109
00:07:13.461 --> 00:07:18.770
The table refreshes every four minutes, and after anything you place or cancel.

110
00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.819
That's Limit Orders: watch what's resting, build ladders with

111
00:07:22.819 --> 00:07:26.735
a full review first, and cancel in bulk when plans change.

